IMPORT prelude

-- National Registry of Diseases Act 2007 (Singapore) -- which diseases are reportable (s 2, the Schedule), which premises are
-- healthcare institutions (s 2), the manager's duty to notify and to supply further information (ss 6, 7), the Registry's duty of
-- confidentiality (ss 5(2), 8), the four routes by which Registry information leaves the Registry (ss 9, 10, 11, 12), the protection
-- of notifiers (s 17(2)), the offences and their maxima (ss 6-9, 10, 12, 14, 18, 23(3)) and composition (s 20).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NRDA2007.txt. The cover says
-- the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; later amendments are annotated in the
-- text, the latest being Act 19 of 2025 (in force 5 December 2025, the Healthcare Services Act definitions in s 2). The deposit's
-- metadata says "Current version as at 03 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0027 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. A patient meets this Act when diagnosed with cancer, kidney failure or a heart attack; a clinic, hospital
-- or laboratory meets it as the institution whose manager must notify.
--
-- Not encoded: appointments (s 3), the Registry's functions (s 4) beyond s 5, investigation powers (ss 13-15) except the obstruction
-- offence, liability of officers of bodies corporate (s 16), protection of officials (s 17(1), (3)), court jurisdiction (s 19),
-- exemptions (s 21), amendment of the Schedule (s 22), the regulation-making list (s 23(1), (2)) and the saving provision (s 24).
-- The FORM and TIME of notification are "prescribed" (s 6(1)) and the regulations were not retrieved, so no deadline is encoded.
-- The case definitions of chronic kidney failure and acute myocardial infarction are in regulations not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text. The writing-l4-rules skill was not loadable in this session, so the
-- conventions of the finished naive rows were followed instead. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no
-- human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Registry of Diseases Act 2007 -- registry`

§§ `2 and the Schedule -- reportable diseases`

-- s 2: "reportable disease" means a disease that is specified in the Schedule. The Schedule: "1. Cancer, including in situ
-- neoplasms, neoplasms with borderline or uncertain malignant potential, as well as all tumours (malignant, borderline, in situ and
-- benign) of the brain and other parts of the central nervous system (including the pituitary gland, craniopharyngeal duct and
-- pineal gland). 2. Single Kidney -- Post Nephrectomy (Donor). 3. Liver -- Post Hepatic Resection (Donor). 4. Chronic kidney
-- failure ... 5. Acute myocardial infarction ..." [S 354/2009; S 529/2009; S 99/2011; S 411/2012]
--
-- A benign tumour is reportable only if it is of the brain or central nervous system. A living kidney or liver donor is on the
-- register although the donor has no disease. Stroke and diabetes are not in the Schedule.
DECLARE Condition IS ONE OF
    `a malignant cancer`
    `an in situ neoplasm`
    `a neoplasm of uncertain malignant potential`
    `a benign brain tumour`
    `a benign pituitary tumour`
    `a benign skin tumour`
    `a single kidney after donating the other`
    `a liver after donating part of it`
    `chronic kidney failure`
    `an acute myocardial infarction`
    `a stroke`
    `diabetes`

GIVEN `the condition` IS A Condition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the condition is a reportable disease` IF
    CONSIDER `the condition`
    WHEN `a benign skin tumour` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a stroke` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `diabetes` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2 -- healthcare institutions`

-- s 2: "healthcare institution" means (a) approved premises or conveyance at which a licensee under the Healthcare Services Act 2020
-- is approved to provide "(i) an acute hospital service; (ii) an ambulatory surgical centre service; (iii) a clinical laboratory
-- service; (iv) a community hospital service; (v) a nuclear medicine service; (vi) an outpatient dental service; (vii) an outpatient
-- medical service; (viii) an outpatient renal dialysis service; (ix) a radiological service; (x) any other licensable healthcare
-- service that may be prescribed"; or (b) anything "declared by the Minister, by order in the Gazette, to be a healthcare
-- institution". [Act 19 of 2025 wef 05/12/2025]
--
-- `a nursing home service` and `a home healthcare service` stand for licensable services NOT in the list; that they are licensable
-- under the Healthcare Services Act 2020 is an inference (that Act was not read for this row).
DECLARE Service IS ONE OF
    `an acute hospital service`
    `an ambulatory surgical centre service`
    `a clinical laboratory service`
    `a community hospital service`
    `a nuclear medicine service`
    `an outpatient dental service`
    `an outpatient medical service`
    `an outpatient renal dialysis service`
    `a radiological service`
    `a nursing home service`
    `a home healthcare service`

GIVEN `the service` IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is listed` IF
    CONSIDER `the service`
    WHEN `a nursing home service` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a home healthcare service` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the service` IS A Service, `the service is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared by Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a healthcare institution` IF
        `the service is listed` `the service`
    OR  `the service is prescribed`
    OR  `declared by Gazette order`

§§ `6 -- the manager's duty to notify`

-- s 6(1): "Where a person is diagnosed with or undergoes treatment for a reportable disease at a healthcare institution, the manager
-- of the healthcare institution must, in the form and within the time prescribed, notify the Registrar of that fact."
-- (2): a manager who "(a) without reasonable excuse, fails to comply" or "(b) ... furnishes as true information which the manager
-- knows or has reason to believe to be false" -- fine not exceeding $2,000. (3): the Registrar's certificate that a notification
-- has not been furnished or is incorrect "is prima facie evidence".
--
-- The duty is the manager's, not the patient's or the treating doctor's. No consent of the patient is asked for.
GIVEN `the condition` IS A Condition, `the service` IS A Service, `the service is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `declared by Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN, `diagnosed or treated there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manager must notify the Registrar` IF
        `diagnosed or treated there`
    AND `the condition is a reportable disease` `the condition`
    AND `it is a healthcare institution` `the service` `the service is prescribed` `declared by Gazette order`

GIVEN `under a duty to notify` IS A BOOLEAN, `notified` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knowingly gave false information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manager commits the s 6 offence` IF
        `under a duty to notify`
    AND (    ((NOT `notified`) AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`))
         OR  `knowingly gave false information`)

§§ `7 -- further information`

-- s 7(1): "Upon a notification being made ... the Registrar or an authorised Registry officer may require the manager ... to provide
-- any additional information that may be prescribed"; (2)(b) including "to produce ... for inspection any medical record".
-- (3): failure without reasonable excuse, or knowingly false information -- fine not exceeding $2,000.
-- s 2 shows the definition of "authorised Registry officer" followed by "[Deleted by Act 11 of 2023 wef 01/05/2023]"; s 7 still uses
-- the term. Whether the annotation refers to that definition or to one removed beside it is not clear from the deposit.
GIVEN `required by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knowingly gave false information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manager commits the s 7 offence` IF
        `required by the Registrar`
    AND (    ((NOT `complied`) AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`))
         OR  `knowingly gave false information`)

§§ `5(2), 8 -- confidentiality`

-- s 5(2): the registers "must not be open for inspection by the public".
-- s 8(1): "Except in the case of a prosecution for an offence under this Act", the Registrar, Registry officers, agents and persons
-- acting under direction "is not compellable in any proceedings to give evidence in respect of, or to produce any document
-- containing, any individually-identifiable information which has been obtained under this Act."
-- s 8(2): "Unless otherwise provided by this Act" they "must not disclose the contents of any register or any individually-
-- identifiable information"; (3) fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both.
DECLARE Proceedings IS ONE OF
    `a prosecution under this Act`
    `a prosecution for murder`
    `a civil negligence claim`
    `a divorce`
    `an insurance dispute`

GIVEN `the proceedings` IS A Proceedings
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Registry officer can be compelled to give identifiable evidence` IF
    CONSIDER `the proceedings`
    WHEN `a prosecution under this Act` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `9, 10, 11, 12 -- how information leaves the Registry`

-- s 9(1): the Registrar "(a) may, on a request by any person and -- (i) upon payment by the person of the prescribed fee; and
-- (ii) subject to the conditions that the Registrar may impose; and (b) must, on a request by the Director-General, disclose or
-- publish any information held by the Registry in an anonymised form." (2): breach of a condition -- $5,000 or 6 months or both.
DECLARE Requester IS ONE OF
    `the Director-General`
    `a member of the public`

DECLARE Answer IS ONE OF
    `must disclose`
    `may disclose`
    `may not disclose`

GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester, `paid the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `the Registrar's answer to a request for anonymised information` IS
    CONSIDER `the requester`
    WHEN `the Director-General` THEN `must disclose`
    WHEN `a member of the public` THEN IF `paid the prescribed fee` THEN `may disclose` ELSE `may not disclose`

-- s 10(1): the Registrar may, with the approval of the Director-General, disclose individually-identifiable information "for the
-- purpose of conducting national public health programmes concerning any reportable disease". (3): the Director-General "must not
-- approve any disclosure ... unless the Director-General is satisfied that the national public health programme cannot be carried
-- out with anonymised information." (7): breach of a condition -- $10,000 or 12 months or both.
-- No consent of the patient is required under s 10 (contrast ss 11, 12, which use "requisite consent").
GIVEN `for a national public health programme on a reportable disease` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Director-General is satisfied anonymised information will not do` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Director-General approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `identifiable information may go to a public health programme` IF
        `for a national public health programme on a reportable disease`
    AND `the Director-General is satisfied anonymised information will not do`
    AND `the Director-General approves`

-- s 11: the Registrar "may, if he or she thinks fit, disclose to a medical practitioner any individually-identifiable information of
-- a medical nature ... if the Registrar is satisfied that -- (a) the medical practitioner is responsible for the treatment and care
-- of that person; (b) the disclosure is necessary for the proper treatment of that person; and (c) the requisite consent has been
-- given". s 2: "medical practitioner" means one registered under the Medical Registration Act 1997 "and who holds a valid
-- practising certificate"; "requisite consent" is the person's own, or, if the person is unable "due to age, infirmity of mind or
-- body or any other cause", that of a person authorised by the regulations.
GIVEN `a registered doctor with a practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN, `responsible for the patient's treatment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `necessary for proper treatment` IS A BOOLEAN, `requisite consent given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may disclose to the treating doctor` IF
        `a registered doctor with a practising certificate`
    AND `responsible for the patient's treatment`
    AND `necessary for proper treatment`
    AND `requisite consent given`

-- s 12(2): the Registrar may disclose identifiable information to a researcher, on conditions and on payment of prescribed fees
-- (if any), if satisfied that "(a) the research cannot be carried out with anonymised information; (b) the requisite consent has been
-- given ...; (c) the research may -- (i) improve the quality of health services ... or (ii) support any national public health
-- policy, initiative or programme concerning any reportable disease; and (d) the researcher and the research comply with the
-- prescribed conditions, if any." (1): the research must be "medical, epidemiological or other form of public health research
-- concerning any reportable disease". (5): a national research advisory committee of "at least 3 and not more than 5 members".
DECLARE `Research application` HAS
    `concerns a reportable disease` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cannot be done with anonymised information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `requisite consent given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `may improve health services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `may support a national public health policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the prescribed conditions` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS A `Research application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may disclose to the researcher` IF
        `the application`'s `concerns a reportable disease`
    AND `the application`'s `cannot be done with anonymised information`
    AND `the application`'s `requisite consent given`
    AND (    `the application`'s `may improve health services`
         OR  `the application`'s `may support a national public health policy`)
    AND `the application`'s `meets the prescribed conditions`

GIVEN `members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advisory committee is properly sized` IF
    `members` AT LEAST 3 AND `members` AT MOST 5

-- s 12(3): the researcher must not "(a) use the individually-identifiable information for any purpose other than the purpose
-- approved by the Registrar; or (b) disclose the name or any other individually-identifiable information of that person unless the
-- requisite consent has been given". (4): nor identify the healthcare institution without the manager's consent, nor the person who
-- provided the information without that person's consent. (6): $10,000 or 12 months or both.
GIVEN `used it for an unapproved purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `named the patient` IS A BOOLEAN, `patient consented to naming` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `named the institution` IS A BOOLEAN, `manager consented to naming` IS A BOOLEAN, `broke a Registrar's condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the researcher commits an offence` IF
        `used it for an unapproved purpose`
    OR  (`named the patient` AND (NOT `patient consented to naming`))
    OR  (`named the institution` AND (NOT `manager consented to naming`))
    OR  `broke a Registrar's condition`

§§ `17(2) -- protection of notifiers`

-- s 17(2): a person who notifies under s 6 or otherwise supplies information to comply with the Act "shall not, by virtue of doing
-- so -- (a) be liable to any suit or other legal proceedings for breach of confidence; or (b) be held ... to have breached any code
-- of professional etiquette or ethics". (Not limited by good faith in the text, unlike s 17(1) and (3).)
-- The good-faith flag is taken and ignored, to make that visible in the cases.
GIVEN `supplied to the Registrar, a Registry officer or agent, or an investigation officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `supplied to comply with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplier is shielded from a breach-of-confidence claim` IF
        `supplied to the Registrar, a Registry officer or agent, or an investigation officer`
    AND `supplied to comply with this Act`

§§ `Offences, maxima and composition`

-- Maxima as stated: s 6(2) and s 7(3) fine $2,000; s 8(3) $10,000 or 12 months; s 9(2) $5,000 or 6 months; s 10(7) $10,000 or
-- 12 months; s 12(6) $10,000 or 12 months; s 14(3) obstructing an investigation officer $5,000 or 6 months; s 18 obstructing the
-- Registrar $5,000 or 6 months; s 23(3) regulations may create offences up to $10,000 or 6 months.
-- s 20(1): the Director-General may compound an offence "that is prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not
-- exceeding the lower of the following -- (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine prescribed for that offence; (b) $5,000."
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to notify (s 6)`
    `failing to give further information (s 7)`
    `Registry disclosure (s 8)`
    `breach of an anonymised-data condition (s 9)`
    `breach of a programme condition (s 10)`
    `researcher misuse (s 12)`
    `obstructing an investigation officer (s 14)`
    `obstructing the Registrar (s 18)`
    `breach of regulations at the maximum (s 23)`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to notify (s 6)` THEN 2000
    WHEN `failing to give further information (s 7)` THEN 2000
    WHEN `Registry disclosure (s 8)` THEN 10000
    WHEN `breach of an anonymised-data condition (s 9)` THEN 5000
    WHEN `breach of a programme condition (s 10)` THEN 10000
    WHEN `researcher misuse (s 12)` THEN 10000
    WHEN `obstructing an investigation officer (s 14)` THEN 5000
    WHEN `obstructing the Registrar (s 18)` THEN 5000
    WHEN `breach of regulations at the maximum (s 23)` THEN 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to notify (s 6)` THEN 0
    WHEN `failing to give further information (s 7)` THEN 0
    WHEN `Registry disclosure (s 8)` THEN 12
    WHEN `breach of an anonymised-data condition (s 9)` THEN 6
    WHEN `breach of a programme condition (s 10)` THEN 12
    WHEN `researcher misuse (s 12)` THEN 12
    WHEN `obstructing an investigation officer (s 14)` THEN 6
    WHEN `obstructing the Registrar (s 18)` THEN 6
    WHEN `breach of regulations at the maximum (s 23)` THEN 6

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be collected on composition` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
